From 7c62393349f75aca61325883a914256c5b943426 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@example.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:03:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(desktop): prewarm also holds remote named profiles used
 in the last 24 h [daveey]

Part B only held each SSH gateway's default profile, so opening a session in a named profile
on the mini (bb-dev, api-*) still waited 9-11 s on a cold per-profile backend (C1 measurement).
RecentRemoteProfiles records every user dispatch's named profile per SSH connection (24 h TTL,
4 per connection, persisted in userData/remote-prewarm-profiles.json); the prewarmer targets
default + those. Also types the always-on lifecycle test results (tsc).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
